1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:01,061
Phil: It's Phil.

2
00:00:01,161 --> 00:00:02,352
Phil: I'm in Pittsburgh.

3
00:00:02,452 --> 00:00:04,902
Phil: The van is confirmed for 8 AM.

4
00:00:05,002 --> 00:00:05,898
Phil: I'll be there.

5
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:09,434
Narrator: His sister has booked a van for Wednesday.

6
00:00:09,534 --> 00:00:11,348
Narrator: She needs his help moving a couch.

7
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:15,723
Narrator: He can reach Pittsburgh.

8
00:00:15,823 --> 00:00:17,630
Narrator: The trouble is getting to Wednesday.

9
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:23,928
Narrator: Alma ran the projectors here for forty-two winters.

10
00:00:24,028 --> 00:00:25,562
Narrator: The Rialto is closing.

11
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:31,290
Narrator: Her daughter lives in Pittsburgh, too.

12
00:00:31,390 --> 00:00:33,173
Narrator: Alma wants her to hear her voice.

13
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:36,304
Larry: I'm coming with you.

14
00:00:36,404 --> 00:00:39,096
Larry: Let's get to the Rialto before the lights go down.

15
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:43,733
Narrator: Larry spends his last camera charge on Alma.

16
00:00:43,833 --> 00:00:46,683
Narrator: Rita makes her own recording and leaves it at the patch.

17
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:49,934
Rita: Phil, the tape is on the patch.

18
00:00:50,034 --> 00:00:51,636
Rita: Larry, the reel is yours.

19
00:00:51,736 --> 00:00:53,711
Rita: I’m going to sit in the dark for a while.

20
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:09,255
Phil: Hi, it's Phil.

21
00:01:09,355 --> 00:01:10,404
Phil: Just checking in.

22
00:01:10,504 --> 00:01:13,265
Phil: The van is confirmed for 8 AM, right?

23
00:01:13,365 --> 00:01:14,806
Phil: I'm in Pittsburgh now.

24
00:01:14,906 --> 00:01:15,803
Phil: I'll be there.

25
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:19,969
Rita: Phil, I’ll handle the transfer from my office later.

26
00:01:20,069 --> 00:01:21,618
Rita: Larry, good luck with the reel.

27
00:01:21,718 --> 00:01:23,127
Rita: I’m stepping out for the night.

28
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:31,960
Narrator: We ran that first morning again.

29
00:01:32,060 --> 00:01:33,849
Narrator: Same town, same promises.

30
00:01:33,949 --> 00:01:35,217
Narrator: Listen to Rita.

31
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:37,340
Rita: The light is right.

32
00:01:37,440 --> 00:01:38,493
Rita: The sound is right.

33
00:01:38,593 --> 00:01:41,291
Rita: Let's get this to her before the reels stop turning.

34
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:46,687
Narrator: Her daughter hears the interview on the first night.

35
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:51,444
Narrator: In another take, Rita went to the dance.

36
00:01:51,544 --> 00:01:53,899
Narrator: Phil had rehearsed the piano all afternoon.

37
00:01:53,999 --> 00:01:55,314
Narrator: He sat at the depot.

38
00:01:57,280 --> 00:01:59,576
Narrator: A writer can screen those lives for a scene.

39
00:01:59,676 --> 00:02:02,319
Narrator: In a game, you could step through the ballroom door yourself.

40
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:09,233
Narrator: Back in our first take, the cinema opens one more time.

41
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:11,850
Rita: Alma.

42
00:02:11,950 --> 00:02:13,129
Rita: I’m bringing the camera.

43
00:02:13,229 --> 00:02:14,269
Rita: We’re doing this now,

44
00:02:14,369 --> 00:02:15,952
Rita: before the reel leaves the building.

45
00:02:16,052 --> 00:02:18,695
Rita: Your daughter needs to hear you, not just see the screen.

46
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:22,930
Larry: It’s done.

47
00:02:23,030 --> 00:02:23,914
Larry: She’s on the tape.

48
00:02:24,014 --> 00:02:24,977
Larry: Tell her it’s real.

49
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:29,101
Phil: I'm here.

50
00:02:29,201 --> 00:02:30,098
Phil: I'll be there.

51
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,206
Rita: It’s done, Larry.

52
00:02:36,306 --> 00:02:37,369
Rita: Don’t touch the reel.

53
00:02:37,469 --> 00:02:38,797
Rita: I’m putting it on the wire.

54
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:49,051
Narrator: The radio still says Tuesday.

55
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:56,800
Written reply: I know that voice. Play it again.
